; Makes EBADENGINE fatal instead of advisory.
;
; Without this, npm prints `npm warn EBADENGINE` for a dependency whose `engines.node` the running
; Node does not satisfy, and then installs anyway and exits 0 — so a below-floor Node is
; indistinguishable from a supported one, and `npm run gate` passes on both. #132 has the
; measurement: jsdom 30 declares `^22.22.2 || ^24.15.0 || >=26.0.0`, CI resolved v22.23.1 and
; emitted zero warnings, and a local v22.17.0 emitted ten and still exited 0.
;
; npm never publishes this file, and `files` is `["dist"]` besides, so it constrains this repo's
; own installs and reaches no consumer.
engine-strict=true
